hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15573","Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman al-Makki narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdullah al-Zuraqi, from his father, he said: And al-Fazari once said: From Ibn Rifah al-Zuraqi, from his father, he said: My father said, and other than al-Fazari said: Ubayd ibn Rifah al-Zuraqi, he said: When it was the day of Uhud and the polytheists turned back, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten until I praise my Lord. So they stood behind him in rows and said: O Allah, to You is all praise. O Allah, none withholds what You spread, nor spreads what You withhold, nor guides whom You lead astray, nor leads astray whom You guide, nor gives what You prevent, nor prevents what You give, nor brings near what You distance, nor distances what You bring near. O Allah, spread upon us of Your blessings and Your mercy and Your bounty and Your provision. O Allah, I ask You the lasting bliss which neither changes nor ceases. O Allah, I ask You bliss on the day of want and security on the day of fear. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You gave us and the evil of what You prevented. O Allah, make belief beloved to us and adorn it in our hearts, and make disbelief and wickedness and disobedience hateful to us, and make us of the rightly guided. O Allah, take us as Muslims and keep us alive as Muslims and join us with the righteous, neither disgraced nor tempted. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who belie Your messengers and bar from Your path, and place upon them Your punishment and Your torment. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who were given the Book, O God of truth."
